1
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:33,000
"Bittersweet Love"

2
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:38,000
(Episode 7)

3
00:01:45,125 --> 00:01:46,392
Is Yun Palace really that huge?

4
00:01:46,416 --> 00:01:48,333
What time did court
officials arrive for duty?

5
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:49,416
Exactly.

6
00:01:49,417 --> 00:01:51,165
No need to envy ancient dignitaries.

7
00:01:51,166 --> 00:01:52,206
They led exhausting lives.

8
00:01:52,291 --> 00:01:54,208
Lüqing is so well-informed.

9
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:55,500
Everything's ready.

10
00:01:55,958 --> 00:01:56,791
Let's eat!

11
00:01:56,792 --> 00:01:58,392
Didn't you say you wanted sugar cruller?

12
00:01:58,750 --> 00:01:59,458
Second Brother.

13
00:01:59,625 --> 00:02:01,500
Lüqing will take me to
see the Forbidden City.

14
00:02:01,541 --> 00:02:02,582
He'll show me

15
00:02:02,583 --> 00:02:04,223
where princesses and consorts once lived.

16
00:02:06,750 --> 00:02:08,000
Lüqing is always busy.

17
00:02:08,083 --> 00:02:09,291
He hardly has time for you.

18
00:02:09,583 --> 00:02:10,583
I'll go with you instead.

19
00:02:10,833 --> 00:02:11,875
I don't want your company.

20
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,165
I've already agreed with Lüqing.

21
00:02:13,166 --> 00:02:14,166
We're going alone.

22
00:02:15,541 --> 00:02:16,166
Mom.

23
00:02:16,541 --> 00:02:17,708
Look at the little one.

24
00:02:17,916 --> 00:02:18,583
It's fine.

25
00:02:18,791 --> 00:02:19,791
They've made a deal.

26
00:02:19,792 --> 00:02:21,000
Just let them go.

27
00:02:34,416 --> 00:02:35,416
Bro.

28
00:02:36,208 --> 00:02:37,333
Are Mom and Dad having fun?

29
00:02:37,916 --> 00:02:38,916
Yeah.

30
00:02:39,125 --> 00:02:40,125
Bro.

31
00:02:40,416 --> 00:02:43,041
Did you really agree to take
her to the Forbidden City?

32
00:02:43,416 --> 00:02:43,875
Mm.

33
00:02:44,208 --> 00:02:45,541
She wants me to take her.

34
00:02:45,916 --> 00:02:47,076
Why don't you take her later?

35
00:02:47,166 --> 00:02:48,166
Mm.

36
00:02:48,750 --> 00:02:49,750
Okay.

37
00:02:50,208 --> 00:02:51,208
It's fine.

38
00:02:57,166 --> 00:02:58,708
Where did this tiny phone come from?

39
00:02:59,541 --> 00:03:01,208
Lüqing got it from abroad.

40
00:03:01,583 --> 00:03:02,875
He accidentally broke it.

41
00:03:02,958 --> 00:03:03,958
So he gave it to me.

42
00:03:04,083 --> 00:03:05,416
I just had it repaired.

43
00:03:06,125 --> 00:03:06,916
Mom, look.
I told you.

44
00:03:08,041 --> 00:03:08,958
The Beis are really wealthy.

45
00:03:08,959 --> 00:03:10,374
This little trinket

46
00:03:10,375 --> 00:03:11,500
must cost tens of thousands.

47
00:03:12,291 --> 00:03:13,666
It's not that expensive.

48
00:03:16,958 --> 00:03:18,290
Our work

49
00:03:18,291 --> 00:03:21,082
keeps us running from
one village to another.

50
00:03:21,083 --> 00:03:22,374
Even just a phone call

51
00:03:22,375 --> 00:03:23,815
can mean a trek of three or four miles.

52
00:03:24,083 --> 00:03:25,000
Not like Fanfan.

53
00:03:25,001 --> 00:03:27,833
He's in the office, just
handling papers and shipments.

54
00:03:29,791 --> 00:03:32,375
A phone like this would sure come in handy!

55
00:03:32,708 --> 00:03:33,708
Don't be so pathetic.

56
00:03:33,833 --> 00:03:36,059
You're always jealous
when your brother gets nice things.

57
00:03:36,083 --> 00:03:37,166
No, Mom, seriously.

58
00:03:37,500 --> 00:03:39,166
When we do promotions,

59
00:03:39,333 --> 00:03:41,101
we have to update our
supervisors all the time.

60
00:03:41,125 --> 00:03:43,166
One mistake with the official stance

61
00:03:43,208 --> 00:03:45,082
can cost us our jobs.

62
00:03:45,083 --> 00:03:46,083
Worse still,

63
00:03:46,291 --> 00:03:47,611
the consequences are unthinkable.

64
00:03:50,125 --> 00:03:52,583
Getting on the leaders’
good side really matters.

65
00:03:53,375 --> 00:03:55,165
Xiaofan, if you don't use it much,

66
00:03:55,166 --> 00:03:56,833
why not give it to your brother?

67
00:03:59,291 --> 00:04:01,291
But this phone belongs to Lüqing.

68
00:04:01,541 --> 00:04:02,832
Didn't Lüqing already give this to you?

69
00:04:02,833 --> 00:04:03,953
What can he do about it now?

70
00:04:04,083 --> 00:04:06,403
Just think of it as me buying
it on installments, alright?

71
00:04:07,125 --> 00:04:08,333
You're brothers!

72
00:04:08,375 --> 00:04:09,655
No need to split yours and mine.

73
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:11,499
When you can afford it later,

74
00:04:11,500 --> 00:04:14,291
just get a new one
and return it to Xiaofan.

75
00:04:14,875 --> 00:04:15,875
Give me back my phone.

76
00:04:16,708 --> 00:04:18,124
Didn't Lüqing give it to you?

77
00:04:18,125 --> 00:04:19,625
Why are you so stingy?

78
00:04:19,875 --> 00:04:23,375
Let me tell you. For Lüqing, getting
another one is just a drop in the bucket.

79
00:04:23,416 --> 00:04:24,832
So giving you one is a piece of cake.

80
00:04:24,833 --> 00:04:26,916
Can't you support your brother's work?

81
00:04:27,083 --> 00:04:29,083
Pingping, give it back to Fanfan.

82
00:04:29,333 --> 00:04:31,083
He'll give it if he likes.

83
00:04:31,125 --> 00:04:32,707
You can't grab it off him.

84
00:04:32,708 --> 00:04:33,828
Are you some kind of robber?

85
00:04:34,125 --> 00:04:35,208
Same goes for you.

86
00:04:35,416 --> 00:04:36,208
How could you

87
00:04:36,209 --> 00:04:37,889
give Xiaofan's things away without asking?

88
00:04:39,750 --> 00:04:42,208
Fanfan just uses his phone for fun.

89
00:04:42,291 --> 00:04:43,958
Pingping relies on it for work.

90
00:04:44,208 --> 00:04:46,208
What's wrong with how I'm handling this?

91
00:04:56,041 --> 00:04:56,958
Hello, who is this?

92
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,541
Why do you have Xiaofan's phone?

93
00:04:58,958 --> 00:05:00,166
Oh, Brother Lüqing.

94
00:05:00,791 --> 00:05:01,791
Give me the phone back.

95
00:05:02,208 --> 00:05:03,291
You're being so petty.

96
00:05:03,958 --> 00:05:04,333
Bro.

97
00:05:04,708 --> 00:05:06,125
Did Lu Xiaoping snatch your phone?

98
00:05:06,208 --> 00:05:09,208
He wanted it; I said no.

99
00:05:09,791 --> 00:05:10,791
I hope that's true.

100
00:05:11,416 --> 00:05:13,708
If Lu Xiaoping takes this phone today,

101
00:05:14,534 --> 00:05:17,361
tomorrow, I'll make him disappear for good.

102
00:05:17,750 --> 00:05:20,540
Pingping's only messing around.

103
00:05:20,541 --> 00:05:22,041
He wouldn't really take my phone.

104
00:05:23,208 --> 00:05:23,500
Bro.

105
00:05:24,166 --> 00:05:26,875
Is there anything else you called about?

106
00:05:27,083 --> 00:05:29,500
I actually wanted to ask you to dinner.

107
00:05:29,750 --> 00:05:31,375
No, thanks.

108
00:05:31,625 --> 00:05:33,855
I promised Lüxin I'd head home for dinner.

109
00:05:34,541 --> 00:05:35,541
Never mind then.

110
00:05:38,083 --> 00:05:39,333
Was Lüqing angry?

111
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:41,500
No.

112
00:05:41,750 --> 00:05:42,333
Mom.

113
00:05:42,708 --> 00:05:44,000
But I really can't

114
00:05:44,416 --> 00:05:46,041
give this phone to Pingping.

115
00:05:47,166 --> 00:05:47,875
I know.

116
00:05:48,166 --> 00:05:49,767
Your brother wants
every nice thing he sees.

117
00:05:49,791 --> 00:05:50,791
Don't do that anymore.

118
00:05:51,541 --> 00:05:52,208
Fine.

119
00:05:52,209 --> 00:05:53,999
I got none of the mutton,

120
00:05:54,000 --> 00:05:55,208
yet I still reek of it.

121
00:05:55,583 --> 00:05:57,583
Should brothers fuss over this?

122
00:05:58,833 --> 00:06:00,208
Married into the Beis,

123
00:06:00,416 --> 00:06:02,541
now you're brothers with Bei Lüqing, huh?

124
00:06:09,291 --> 00:06:10,375
You stubborn old fool!

125
00:06:10,416 --> 00:06:11,541
What exactly are you after?

126
00:06:12,125 --> 00:06:12,916
Back home,

127
00:06:13,083 --> 00:06:14,726
you threw a fit begging to come to Yunjing,

128
00:06:14,750 --> 00:06:16,708
Yet now you're the one moping around.

129
00:06:17,541 --> 00:06:18,541
We're here,

130
00:06:18,625 --> 00:06:20,833
and Xiaofan took time off
work just to show us around.

131
00:06:21,083 --> 00:06:22,083
Just look at you,

132
00:06:22,583 --> 00:06:24,208
moping all day.

133
00:06:24,375 --> 00:06:25,375
Who's this long face for?

134
00:06:26,458 --> 00:06:27,698
It's our first time in Yunjing,

135
00:06:27,833 --> 00:06:28,916
and all along

136
00:06:29,333 --> 00:06:31,000
he's been siding with strangers.

137
00:06:32,125 --> 00:06:33,332
Xiaofan doesn't owe our family a thing.

138
00:06:33,333 --> 00:06:34,333
Get that straight.

139
00:06:35,791 --> 00:06:36,791
Oh right, Dad.

140
00:06:37,625 --> 00:06:40,500
We haven't had Peking
duck in Yunjing yet, have we?

141
00:06:40,583 --> 00:06:41,208
Right, Dad.

142
00:06:41,333 --> 00:06:43,540
This is a rare delicacy in Yunjing.

143
00:06:43,541 --> 00:06:46,828
If you've never tasted it, the folks at
home will think you never set foot here.

144
00:06:47,208 --> 00:06:49,166
It's just duck. What's the big deal?

145
00:06:49,601 --> 00:06:52,392
I'm country folk, but I've had duck.

146
00:06:52,416 --> 00:06:54,041
Dad, this is actually quite different.

147
00:06:54,416 --> 00:06:56,374
The Beis only eat duck skin.

148
00:06:56,375 --> 00:06:57,615
No one cares much for the meat.

149
00:06:57,708 --> 00:06:59,416
The skin's golden and glossy.

150
00:07:02,708 --> 00:07:03,708
I want some.

151
00:07:04,416 --> 00:07:05,934
The kids act out of genuine filial respect.

152
00:07:05,958 --> 00:07:07,625
If you won't eat, I will.

153
00:07:08,125 --> 00:07:09,125
Let's go.

154
00:07:13,333 --> 00:07:14,333
You're finally here.

155
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:15,500
Um.

156
00:07:15,685 --> 00:07:17,184
Do you still have a private room?

157
00:07:17,208 --> 00:07:19,082
Not for others, but for you we do.

158
00:07:19,083 --> 00:07:20,708
Don't worry, everything's all arranged.

159
00:07:21,333 --> 00:07:23,093
I'll take you to the
private room right now.

160
00:07:36,208 --> 00:07:36,625
Dad.

161
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,000
Look at this.

162
00:07:40,416 --> 00:07:41,166
Here, here, here.

163
00:07:41,208 --> 00:07:42,208
Put it here, right here.

164
00:07:43,875 --> 00:07:45,416
I haven't placed our order yet.

165
00:07:46,541 --> 00:07:48,499
Way classier than the Beis.

166
00:07:48,500 --> 00:07:49,540
The Beis go for Western decor,

167
00:07:49,541 --> 00:07:50,291
while this place is all Chinese style.
Totally different.

168
00:07:51,708 --> 00:07:52,166
Eat up.
It's delicious, Dad, really tasty.

169
00:07:53,167 --> 00:07:54,833
Why's this private room so loud?

170
00:07:58,625 --> 00:07:59,625
Brother Lüqing.

171
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,000
Bro.

172
00:08:04,916 --> 00:08:05,916
Now I get it.

173
00:08:06,041 --> 00:08:07,791
No wonder you picked this spot to treat me.

174
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:09,375
You've got other people here,

175
00:08:09,500 --> 00:08:10,875
I'm just an afterthought.

176
00:08:11,416 --> 00:08:12,125
Lüqing.

177
00:08:12,291 --> 00:08:13,291
Over here, come on!

178
00:08:13,333 --> 00:08:14,333
Come sit.

179
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,000
Let's go.

180
00:08:20,708 --> 00:08:21,166
Waiter.
Two more sets, please.

181
00:08:29,583 --> 00:08:30,583
Xiaofan.

182
00:08:30,625 --> 00:08:32,000
Didn't you say you'd eat at home?

183
00:08:33,250 --> 00:08:35,958
I just realized I've never brought
my dad here for roast duck.

184
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:37,000
So we came.

185
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:41,083
No wonder

186
00:08:41,541 --> 00:08:44,166
the manager said I was
late as soon as he saw me.

187
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:46,165
I see, you reserved the room beforehand.

188
00:08:46,166 --> 00:08:47,166
Thanks.

189
00:08:48,208 --> 00:08:49,208
Sorry,

190
00:08:49,500 --> 00:08:50,500
to crash your gathering.

191
00:08:50,750 --> 00:08:54,291
How about I ask the manager
to get us another private room?

192
00:08:55,791 --> 00:08:56,791
No trouble at all!

193
00:08:56,916 --> 00:08:58,836
This room was booked
for you in the first place.

194
00:08:59,375 --> 00:09:00,125
I ordered a bunch of dishes already,

195
00:09:00,126 --> 00:09:01,184
and they can’t be cancelled.

196
00:09:01,208 --> 00:09:02,540
You said you weren't
coming when I rang earlier,

197
00:09:02,541 --> 00:09:03,541
so that's why I brought...

198
00:09:04,791 --> 00:09:05,791
Since you're all here,

199
00:09:05,875 --> 00:09:06,750
let's dig in.
Don't let it go to waste.

200
00:09:08,125 --> 00:09:09,083
Don't take offense.

201
00:09:09,125 --> 00:09:11,208
My little brother's just naturally shy.

202
00:09:11,370 --> 00:09:12,374
He gets flustered

203
00:09:12,375 --> 00:09:13,750
around new people.

204
00:09:14,833 --> 00:09:17,375
Xiaofan and I go way back.

205
00:09:17,708 --> 00:09:18,750
We're hardly strangers.

206
00:09:19,375 --> 00:09:20,000
Oh, really?

207
00:09:20,001 --> 00:09:21,761
Any friend of Xiaofan's
is a friend of mine.

208
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,083
Here’s to you!

209
00:09:35,159 --> 00:09:36,159
Bro.

210
00:09:36,291 --> 00:09:37,707
What line of work are you in?

211
00:09:37,708 --> 00:09:39,500
I run a securities business in Gangcheng.

212
00:09:41,083 --> 00:09:42,915
Gangcheng's stock market

213
00:09:42,916 --> 00:09:45,708
must be way more thrilling
than the mainland's, right?

214
00:09:45,791 --> 00:09:46,916
Here's to you again.

215
00:09:57,541 --> 00:09:59,125
Did you have a good time today?

216
00:10:01,208 --> 00:10:03,166
It was... good. It was good.

217
00:10:09,916 --> 00:10:10,333
Bro.

218
00:10:10,500 --> 00:10:12,916
I'll reach out to you about stocks later.

219
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:14,500
Bottoms up.

220
00:10:19,083 --> 00:10:20,083
Come on, come on.

221
00:10:20,166 --> 00:10:21,166
Dig in, everyone!

222
00:10:21,375 --> 00:10:22,583
Don't only drink.

223
00:10:23,333 --> 00:10:25,500
Dad, Mom, help yourselves.

224
00:10:26,916 --> 00:10:27,375
Don't hold me up.

225
00:10:27,376 --> 00:10:28,500
This is so embarrassing.

226
00:10:28,708 --> 00:10:29,708
Good grief.

227
00:10:30,416 --> 00:10:31,416
Oh dear.

228
00:10:44,041 --> 00:10:45,041
Bro.

229
00:10:45,666 --> 00:10:46,791
Sorry about today.

230
00:10:53,541 --> 00:10:54,583
If you've got other plans,

231
00:10:55,625 --> 00:10:56,625
go on ahead.

232
00:11:26,041 --> 00:11:27,041
Brother.

233
00:11:27,375 --> 00:11:28,375
Where's Bei Lüqing?

234
00:11:29,750 --> 00:11:30,750
He left.

235
00:11:33,375 --> 00:11:34,375
He's gone?

236
00:11:34,791 --> 00:11:36,751
Is he still gonna take me
to Yun Palace tomorrow?

237
00:11:38,750 --> 00:11:39,750
Don't be so childish.

238
00:11:39,875 --> 00:11:41,155
Lüqing's got a lot on his plate.

239
00:11:42,125 --> 00:11:44,375
I think you upset Lüqing.

240
00:11:44,708 --> 00:11:46,541
Lüqing always keeps his word.

241
00:11:48,041 --> 00:11:49,125
Go check on your brother.

242
00:11:49,375 --> 00:11:51,125
You're a girl with no self-respect.

243
00:11:55,375 --> 00:11:56,655
A girl grown up is hard to keep.

244
00:12:02,333 --> 00:12:03,333
Fanfan.

245
00:12:04,375 --> 00:12:05,375
C'mon, sit by me.

246
00:12:17,291 --> 00:12:18,291
Fanfan.

247
00:12:19,125 --> 00:12:20,125
It's my fault.

248
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:21,860
I've put you through so much hurt.

249
00:12:22,541 --> 00:12:23,625
That's not true.

250
00:12:23,875 --> 00:12:24,875
Mom.

251
00:12:25,333 --> 00:12:26,708
I'm doing perfectly well here.

252
00:12:28,125 --> 00:12:29,125
Truth be told,

253
00:12:29,333 --> 00:12:31,413
I forced you to marry into
another family years ago.

254
00:12:31,916 --> 00:12:33,083
I thought

255
00:12:33,125 --> 00:12:34,625
you'd be our lifeline,

256
00:12:34,958 --> 00:12:36,541
a way to get all your siblings

257
00:12:36,916 --> 00:12:39,500
out of our poor little mountain hollow.

258
00:12:40,291 --> 00:12:42,131
I originally wanted your
eldest brother to go.

259
00:12:42,375 --> 00:12:43,541
Being the oldest,

260
00:12:44,041 --> 00:12:45,801
that responsibility
should've fallen to him.

261
00:12:46,875 --> 00:12:49,291
But they chose you out of everyone.

262
00:12:51,500 --> 00:12:52,375
Looking back now,

263
00:12:52,376 --> 00:12:53,536
it's a good thing it was you.

264
00:12:54,541 --> 00:12:55,708
You could endure hardship,

265
00:12:56,208 --> 00:12:57,583
and you got on well with everyone.

266
00:12:58,083 --> 00:12:59,163
Unlike your oldest brother,

267
00:12:59,541 --> 00:13:01,061
he's got his head stuck in the clouds.

268
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Truth be told,

269
00:13:07,083 --> 00:13:09,375
I've come here for your little sister.

270
00:13:11,375 --> 00:13:13,083
She's of marrying age.

271
00:13:13,416 --> 00:13:14,833
With our city ties,

272
00:13:15,166 --> 00:13:16,707
she won't settle for
anyone back in the village.

273
00:13:16,708 --> 00:13:18,474
She won't settle but
she's not much of a catch.

274
00:13:18,750 --> 00:13:20,333
If we can't get your sister sorted out,

275
00:13:20,541 --> 00:13:22,541
she's gonna be a huge
headache for you eventually.

276
00:13:24,416 --> 00:13:25,458
So I was wondering

277
00:13:25,750 --> 00:13:27,208
if you could ask around

278
00:13:27,541 --> 00:13:29,833
and see if any families in
town are looking for a wife,

279
00:13:30,291 --> 00:13:31,892
someone willing to take our youngest girl.

280
00:13:31,916 --> 00:13:33,625
We don't need a rich family.

281
00:13:34,208 --> 00:13:35,708
An ordinary one is enough,

282
00:13:36,500 --> 00:13:38,220
as long as they don't mistreat your sister.

283
00:13:42,208 --> 00:13:43,708
Why look any further?

284
00:13:43,916 --> 00:13:47,583
Just look at how well Lüqing
and his little sister get along.

285
00:13:48,208 --> 00:13:50,833
Lüqing has always treated
your little sister well.

286
00:13:51,916 --> 00:13:56,416
Didn't you once say Lüqing had a
bit of a crush on your little sister?

287
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,000
Fanfan.

288
00:14:00,541 --> 00:14:02,541
I don't have to have Lüqing for her.

289
00:14:02,875 --> 00:14:04,958
I just want you to help and ask him,

290
00:14:05,166 --> 00:14:07,291
if he likes your sister at all.

291
00:14:07,791 --> 00:14:09,374
Women marry up,

292
00:14:09,375 --> 00:14:10,375
men marry down.

293
00:14:11,166 --> 00:14:12,934
It's completely common
for the bride to come from

294
00:14:12,958 --> 00:14:14,718
a less privileged
background than the groom.

295
00:14:21,083 --> 00:14:22,582
If he doesn't have feelings for her,

296
00:14:22,583 --> 00:14:23,625
we won't push it.

297
00:14:24,041 --> 00:14:26,041
Just ask around for other families.

298
00:14:27,541 --> 00:14:28,541
Mom.

299
00:14:31,208 --> 00:14:32,583
I get what you're saying.

300
00:14:37,541 --> 00:14:38,541
So

301
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:42,708
we want her to stay here a
few extra days when we leave.

302
00:14:43,125 --> 00:14:45,583
Let them spend time to know each other.

303
00:14:47,541 --> 00:14:48,541
Dream on.

304
00:14:52,166 --> 00:14:53,166
Lüxin.

305
00:14:54,875 --> 00:14:55,875
You're at home.

306
00:14:58,166 --> 00:15:00,541
Get your family out of
my house this instant.

307
00:15:02,375 --> 00:15:04,583
Lüxin, we're just kidding.

308
00:15:07,333 --> 00:15:08,333
Just a joke?

309
00:15:09,166 --> 00:15:10,541
I meant every word.

310
00:15:11,375 --> 00:15:12,707
Leave right now.

311
00:15:12,708 --> 00:15:14,388
Never set foot in the Bei household again.

312
00:15:14,625 --> 00:15:16,749
You're kicking us out now?

313
00:15:16,750 --> 00:15:19,374
But who came to our house to propose,

314
00:15:19,375 --> 00:15:20,750
eager to marry into our family?

315
00:15:23,208 --> 00:15:24,541
You feel wronged?

316
00:15:26,041 --> 00:15:27,801
If you feel wronged,
don't get married then.

317
00:15:28,500 --> 00:15:29,500
Who forced you?

318
00:15:31,875 --> 00:15:32,833
You've gained plenty

319
00:15:32,834 --> 00:15:34,166
from this marriage, haven't you?

320
00:15:34,875 --> 00:15:35,875
Otherwise,

321
00:15:36,208 --> 00:15:39,833
how did every piecce of trash
from your family sneak into Yunjing?

322
00:15:43,166 --> 00:15:44,208
Who are you calling trash?

323
00:15:45,291 --> 00:15:46,291
Who?

324
00:15:46,833 --> 00:15:48,583
Anyone who's fucking trash.

325
00:15:48,708 --> 00:15:50,583
I'm talking about shameless trash.

326
00:15:50,875 --> 00:15:52,750
Too vain to look at their own reflection.

327
00:15:53,875 --> 00:15:56,500
Our families should've never gotten married.

328
00:15:57,125 --> 00:15:58,999
You carried another
man's kid before you wed.

329
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,624
Shameless yourself, yet you judge others.

330
00:16:01,625 --> 00:16:02,625
Zhenxing.

331
00:16:05,541 --> 00:16:06,541
That's right.

332
00:16:07,541 --> 00:16:09,541
Sure, I was pregnant and
hunting for a scapegoat,

333
00:16:10,375 --> 00:16:13,581
but it takes a willing party
to pawn off their own son!

334
00:16:14,541 --> 00:16:16,341
So I'm shameless for
marrying while pregnant?

335
00:16:17,208 --> 00:16:19,083
You knew I was carrying
another man's child,

336
00:16:19,208 --> 00:16:20,684
but you still sold your boy to me anyway.

337
00:16:20,708 --> 00:16:23,000
The real shameless person here is you.

338
00:16:24,291 --> 00:16:24,708
You...
Zhenxing.

339
00:16:25,376 --> 00:16:26,583
Zhenxing! Zhenxing!

340
00:16:27,291 --> 00:16:28,291
Brother.

341
00:16:28,625 --> 00:16:29,166
Brother.

342
00:16:29,208 --> 00:16:30,540
Why don't you beat your wife?

343
00:16:30,541 --> 00:16:32,291
Look how she speaks to Mom!

344
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:33,541
Hit me?

345
00:16:34,208 --> 00:16:35,707
Your brother's just my doorman,

346
00:16:35,708 --> 00:16:36,767
yet I still can't stand the sight of him.

347
00:16:36,791 --> 00:16:38,791
Wonder why I haven't tossed him out?

348
00:16:39,375 --> 00:16:40,415
Simple. I, Bei Lüxin,

349
00:16:40,416 --> 00:16:42,500
don't burn bridges.

350
00:16:42,541 --> 00:16:43,916
What are you so smug about?

351
00:16:44,083 --> 00:16:45,958
You think you're my family or something?

352
00:16:46,208 --> 00:16:47,208
Get the hell out.

353
00:16:47,791 --> 00:16:48,833
You're a disgrace.

354
00:16:49,166 --> 00:16:50,833
Get the hell out, now.

355
00:16:58,458 --> 00:17:00,125
I'll kill you! I'll kill you!

356
00:17:18,208 --> 00:17:19,541
Cut it out, all of you!

357
00:17:20,708 --> 00:17:21,708
Stop!

358
00:17:41,125 --> 00:17:42,125
Mom.

359
00:17:42,750 --> 00:17:43,750
Dad.

360
00:17:45,208 --> 00:17:46,541
I'm sending you off this minute.

361
00:18:13,750 --> 00:18:14,875
Bro.

362
00:18:14,898 --> 00:18:15,398
Hello?

363
00:18:16,083 --> 00:18:17,083
Who's this?

364
00:18:38,958 --> 00:18:39,958
Lüxin,

365
00:18:40,291 --> 00:18:41,625
all these years,

366
00:18:42,041 --> 00:18:44,375
we’ve been living separate lives.

367
00:18:44,833 --> 00:18:47,041
We haven’t been real
husband and wife for ages.

368
00:19:09,375 --> 00:19:11,455
I forced you to marry into
another family years ago.

369
00:19:11,625 --> 00:19:14,416
I thought you'd be our lifeline,

370
00:19:14,708 --> 00:19:16,208
a way to get all your siblings

371
00:19:16,416 --> 00:19:18,875
out of our poor little mountain hollow.

372
00:19:22,916 --> 00:19:23,916
Lüxin,

373
00:19:24,916 --> 00:19:26,791
don't blame Mom and Dad.

374
00:19:27,833 --> 00:19:30,666
My arrival has caused trouble for everyone.

375
00:19:33,125 --> 00:19:34,125
Xiaofan.

376
00:19:34,750 --> 00:19:36,750
I'll be staying at
Lüqing's place for a while.

377
00:19:37,541 --> 00:19:38,541
So...

378
00:19:38,833 --> 00:19:40,833
I'm afraid I'll have to
ask you to move out.

379
00:19:41,333 --> 00:19:43,457
Lüxin, I think

380
00:19:43,458 --> 00:19:45,000
we should get a divorce.

381
00:19:46,166 --> 00:19:49,500
On the grounds of... irreconcilable differences.

382
00:19:50,208 --> 00:19:53,541
With an amicable mutual separation.

383
00:20:38,291 --> 00:20:38,958
Xiaofan.

384
00:20:39,208 --> 00:20:40,208
What are you doing here?

385
00:20:40,791 --> 00:20:42,416
Didn't you take a week off?

386
00:20:42,916 --> 00:20:44,416
Didn't you say earlier

387
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:46,708
you wanted to send a sales rep to Lingang?

388
00:20:47,083 --> 00:20:48,583
Yes, that's right.

389
00:20:51,208 --> 00:20:52,374
Listen, Xiaofan.

390
00:20:52,375 --> 00:20:53,749
The treatment there is terrible

391
00:20:53,750 --> 00:20:55,207
with zero room for advancement.

392
00:20:55,208 --> 00:20:56,915
Don't let your friend wade into this mess.

393
00:20:56,916 --> 00:20:57,916
No.

394
00:20:58,208 --> 00:21:01,375
I want to go there myself.

395
00:21:02,304 --> 00:21:02,877
What?

396
00:21:03,125 --> 00:21:04,000
You're giving up the office job?

397
00:21:04,001 --> 00:21:05,375
You wanna work out in the field?

398
00:21:08,208 --> 00:21:10,291
You're stepping down on purpose.

399
00:21:10,375 --> 00:21:12,332
There's no precedent for
this in our organization.

400
00:21:12,333 --> 00:21:13,653
I'll file the application myself.

401
00:21:14,041 --> 00:21:15,375
If anything goes wrong,

402
00:21:15,541 --> 00:21:17,181
Section Chief, it won't be on you at all.

403
00:21:18,041 --> 00:21:20,333
Xiaofan, think long and hard about this.

404
00:21:20,870 --> 00:21:22,700
I'll level with you now.

405
00:21:23,166 --> 00:21:25,540
If you leave and later want to come back,

406
00:21:25,541 --> 00:21:27,083
I won't have the final say anymore.

407
00:21:27,625 --> 00:21:28,625
Also,

408
00:21:30,208 --> 00:21:31,790
discuss this with your spouse

409
00:21:31,791 --> 00:21:33,017
before submitting your request.

410
00:21:33,041 --> 00:21:34,041
Alright?

411
00:21:34,125 --> 00:21:35,125
Thank you, Section Chief.

412
00:21:43,875 --> 00:21:44,875
Xiaofan.

413
00:21:45,166 --> 00:21:46,166
Dad's asking for you.

414
00:21:51,291 --> 00:21:52,291
You've gone too far.

415
00:21:53,208 --> 00:21:54,874
What gives you the
right to belittle someone

416
00:21:54,875 --> 00:21:57,041
who's never criticized your past?

417
00:21:57,708 --> 00:21:59,958
Just apologize to Xiaofan.

418
00:22:00,583 --> 00:22:04,125
He just needs an out to save face.

419
00:22:04,791 --> 00:22:05,875
Say sorry,

420
00:22:06,208 --> 00:22:07,958
spouses don't keep overnight grudges.

421
00:22:11,125 --> 00:22:14,166
Xiaofan, come over, sit down.

422
00:22:20,125 --> 00:22:22,125
Sit down, let's talk properly.

423
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:29,291
Let's have a family meeting today.

424
00:22:30,041 --> 00:22:31,041
First of all,

425
00:22:31,958 --> 00:22:33,166
I must reprimand Lüxin.

426
00:22:34,750 --> 00:22:37,375
First off, you're rude to your elders.

427
00:22:38,208 --> 00:22:40,916
Your in-laws are your parents.

428
00:22:41,208 --> 00:22:43,415
No one kicks their own parents

429
00:22:43,416 --> 00:22:44,708
out of the house.

430
00:22:45,541 --> 00:22:46,541
Second off,

431
00:22:47,208 --> 00:22:49,375
you don't respect your husband one bit!

432
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:55,120
It's my fault as well.
I've been far too busy working.

433
00:22:55,625 --> 00:22:58,541
Plus your mom’s never been around.

434
00:22:59,125 --> 00:23:00,791
So I spoiled you too much.

435
00:23:01,750 --> 00:23:02,875
On that note,

436
00:23:03,291 --> 00:23:04,375
I have to blame myself too.

437
00:23:05,416 --> 00:23:06,416
Dad.

438
00:23:06,750 --> 00:23:08,000
This isn't your fault.

439
00:23:09,375 --> 00:23:12,504
I also don't hate Lüxin,
and that's not why I want a divorce.

440
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:16,083
Why on earth do you
want to divorce Bei Lüxin?

441
00:23:22,416 --> 00:23:23,708
Actually, I've thought it over.

442
00:23:24,750 --> 00:23:26,291
Lüxin's right.

443
00:23:27,958 --> 00:23:29,358
I'm really not good enough for her.

444
00:23:30,125 --> 00:23:33,583
Whether it's education, appearance,
capability or background,

445
00:23:34,125 --> 00:23:35,245
I'm worthless on all counts.

446
00:23:37,875 --> 00:23:40,083
I don't want to keep wasting her time.

447
00:23:41,791 --> 00:23:43,875
I'm truly thankful

448
00:23:45,791 --> 00:23:47,111
for all your help over the years.

449
00:23:49,208 --> 00:23:51,791
I don't wanna keep
being a burden to you all.

450
00:23:52,750 --> 00:23:53,750
Does your mom

451
00:23:54,041 --> 00:23:55,041
know about this?

452
00:23:57,583 --> 00:23:58,583
They don't know.

453
00:23:59,625 --> 00:24:01,041
This is my own decision.

454
00:24:01,166 --> 00:24:02,958
Talk it over with your mother first.

455
00:24:03,166 --> 00:24:05,166
Get your elders’ input too.

456
00:24:05,666 --> 00:24:06,666
Dad.

457
00:24:07,707 --> 00:24:09,332
I married Lüxin

458
00:24:09,750 --> 00:24:11,333
on my elders’ advice.

459
00:24:12,125 --> 00:24:13,125
This time...

460
00:24:13,652 --> 00:24:14,736
just let it be.

461
00:24:16,416 --> 00:24:17,776
If he wants a divorce, fine by me.

462
00:24:18,708 --> 00:24:20,333
As if I care about Lu Xiaofan!

463
00:24:32,291 --> 00:24:33,291
Dad.

464
00:24:33,416 --> 00:24:34,833
I'm going to my room.

465
00:24:38,416 --> 00:24:39,416
Bro.

466
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:41,000
Can you come for a bit?

467
00:24:42,041 --> 00:24:43,241
I've got a few things for you.

468
00:24:51,083 --> 00:24:52,083
In here,

469
00:24:53,375 --> 00:24:55,541
there's the scarf you
brought me from France,

470
00:24:56,708 --> 00:24:58,416
plus the CD player you gifted me.

471
00:25:01,541 --> 00:25:02,625
Oh,

472
00:25:16,500 --> 00:25:17,750
and this one too.

473
00:25:21,416 --> 00:25:22,416
Bro.

474
00:25:24,083 --> 00:25:25,791
Lüxin and I are getting divorced.

475
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:32,125
I don't deserve all these nice things.

476
00:25:35,875 --> 00:25:36,875
I see.

477
00:25:38,416 --> 00:25:39,416
Lu Xiaofan.

478
00:25:40,541 --> 00:25:42,291
This isn't just a divorce from Bei Lüxin.

479
00:25:45,541 --> 00:25:47,916
You want to cut all contact with the Beis.

480
00:25:52,333 --> 00:25:54,083
These things aren't worth much.

481
00:25:54,708 --> 00:25:55,708
If you don't want them,

482
00:25:56,083 --> 00:25:57,625
just toss ’em in the trash.

483
00:26:12,750 --> 00:26:13,750
Xiaofan.

484
00:26:13,958 --> 00:26:15,166
I don't agree to

485
00:26:15,916 --> 00:26:17,083
this divorce.

486
00:26:18,875 --> 00:26:20,583
If you just need some time apart,

487
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:22,000
that's okay.

488
00:26:23,166 --> 00:26:25,208
It'll give everyone time to calm down.

489
00:26:25,916 --> 00:26:27,416
Once everyone's cooled off,

490
00:26:27,541 --> 00:26:28,541
we'll talk again.

491
00:26:34,375 --> 00:26:35,375
Dad.

492
00:26:35,833 --> 00:26:37,083
I'll be going now.

493
00:27:00,458 --> 00:27:01,458
Lingang?

494
00:27:02,166 --> 00:27:03,646
The climate's the same as in Yunjing.

495
00:27:04,041 --> 00:27:05,500
Your lips get dry easily.

496
00:27:06,000 --> 00:27:07,416
Make some soup for yourself.

497
00:27:35,208 --> 00:27:37,082
Maybe he's just a rich kid

498
00:27:37,083 --> 00:27:38,500
padding his resume.

499
00:27:39,125 --> 00:27:41,500
He volunteered to come down from Yunjing.

500
00:27:41,833 --> 00:27:43,165
Probably got himself into trouble.

501
00:27:43,166 --> 00:27:44,332
None of our concern, then.

502
00:27:44,333 --> 00:27:46,750
Thing is, our section
chief's retiring soon.

503
00:27:47,208 --> 00:27:48,601
Right as our chief's set to retire,

504
00:27:48,625 --> 00:27:49,790
a well-connected higher official

505
00:27:49,791 --> 00:27:51,416
lands here out of nowhere.

506
00:27:53,541 --> 00:27:54,541
Wang.

507
00:27:55,083 --> 00:27:56,915
Is he gonna snatch your promotion?

508
00:27:56,916 --> 00:27:57,916
Don't talk nonsense.

509
00:27:57,958 --> 00:27:58,999
Even after the chief retires,

510
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:00,541
it might not be my turn.

511
00:28:00,791 --> 00:28:03,000
But I dug up info on Lu Xiaofan,

512
00:28:03,166 --> 00:28:04,875
apparently he’s a live-in son-in-law.

513
00:28:06,375 --> 00:28:07,375
Alright, drop it.

514
00:28:07,750 --> 00:28:08,708
Stop gossiping
and mind your own work.

515
00:28:10,583 --> 00:28:13,625
Our department's been dead
last in performance six months running.

516
00:28:14,083 --> 00:28:15,625
At this pace, forget promotions,

517
00:28:16,125 --> 00:28:17,500
we could lose our jobs.

518
00:28:19,208 --> 00:28:20,333
Miss Xu.

519
00:28:20,416 --> 00:28:21,624
What's that supposed to mean?

520
00:28:21,625 --> 00:28:23,184
You'd actually go for a live-in son-in-law?

521
00:28:23,208 --> 00:28:23,875
Exactly.
Alright, alright.

522
00:28:24,792 --> 00:28:25,999
Stay focused while on the clock.

523
00:28:26,000 --> 00:28:27,000
Back to work, everyone.

524
00:29:02,000 --> 00:29:03,601
It wasn't until Lu Xiaofan came to Lingang

525
00:29:03,625 --> 00:29:05,416
that he began a brand-new life.

526
00:29:06,416 --> 00:29:08,083
Sitting in the office all day,

527
00:29:08,208 --> 00:29:10,333
relaying updates to the company.

528
00:29:10,583 --> 00:29:12,375
Nothing much to do, honestly.

529
00:29:13,708 --> 00:29:15,125
In the spring of 1995,

530
00:29:15,208 --> 00:29:16,750
stock speculation frenzy hit its peak.

531
00:29:18,333 --> 00:29:20,916
In his spare time, he
skimmed stock newspapers.

532
00:29:21,208 --> 00:29:22,708
After hours,

533
00:29:22,750 --> 00:29:25,083
he wanted a Langjian Securities account

534
00:29:25,833 --> 00:29:28,208
to catch the market wave.

535
00:29:28,541 --> 00:29:28,958
Hello.

536
00:29:29,458 --> 00:29:30,000
Hello.

537
00:29:30,001 --> 00:29:31,121
I'd like to open an account.

538
00:29:37,958 --> 00:29:39,000
Isn't that Xiaofan?

539
00:29:39,416 --> 00:29:41,375
Xiaofan! Xiaofan!

540
00:29:46,916 --> 00:29:47,916
Ziyang.

541
00:29:48,375 --> 00:29:49,375
And this is...

542
00:29:49,875 --> 00:29:51,208
This is Lüxin's husband.

543
00:29:51,916 --> 00:29:53,196
Let me introduce him to you two.

544
00:29:53,416 --> 00:29:55,249
This is Langjian's general manager.

545
00:29:55,250 --> 00:29:56,250
Lu Tao.

546
00:29:56,375 --> 00:29:57,166
Same family name as you.

547
00:29:57,208 --> 00:29:58,208
Just get acquainted.

548
00:29:58,375 --> 00:29:59,958
I was thinking this morning,

549
00:30:00,041 --> 00:30:01,641
why were there magpies chirping outside?

550
00:30:03,083 --> 00:30:03,625
Lu Tao.

551
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:05,000
Oh.

552
00:30:05,291 --> 00:30:06,291
Hello.

553
00:30:06,416 --> 00:30:07,856
Arrange a VIP trading booth for him.

554
00:30:08,833 --> 00:30:09,993
No, no, that's not necessary.

555
00:30:11,208 --> 00:30:12,208
Naturally.

556
00:30:12,375 --> 00:30:14,416
Otherwise we can't
explain ourselves to Lüqing.

557
00:30:15,166 --> 00:30:16,166
There's really no need.

558
00:30:16,416 --> 00:30:17,000
Ziyang.
Mr. Lu.

559
00:30:17,833 --> 00:30:19,313
I have to run, I've got things to do.

560
00:30:26,166 --> 00:30:27,458
You're kidding me, right?

561
00:30:28,291 --> 00:30:29,411
Bei Lüqing's brother-in-law?

562
00:30:30,958 --> 00:30:32,040
Given how powerful Bei Lüqing is,

563
00:30:32,041 --> 00:30:33,708
how'd his sister wind up with a nobody?

564
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:36,666
I swear I'm not lying, cross my heart.

565
00:30:37,500 --> 00:30:38,625
And listen,

566
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:40,040
he has plenty of influence

567
00:30:40,083 --> 00:30:41,083
over Lüqing.

568
00:30:41,708 --> 00:30:43,916
If you're trying to
lure Lüqing to Langjian,

569
00:30:44,708 --> 00:30:46,333
drag him into the game first.

570
00:30:46,750 --> 00:30:47,750
Trust me.

571
00:30:47,958 --> 00:30:50,132
Not only will it work,
but it'll work fast too.

572
00:30:50,750 --> 00:30:52,188
Unbelievable.

573
00:30:52,750 --> 00:30:54,625
I always figured someone like Bei Lüqing

574
00:30:55,208 --> 00:30:56,833
couldn't be swayed

575
00:30:58,708 --> 00:30:59,708
by anyone.

576
00:31:02,083 --> 00:31:03,083
Don't worry.

577
00:31:04,208 --> 00:31:05,328
If there's money to be made,

578
00:31:06,208 --> 00:31:07,208
you'll get your share.

579
00:31:08,375 --> 00:31:09,458
This is nothing.

580
00:31:09,625 --> 00:31:11,541
Brothers don't nitpick over tiny sums.

581
00:31:12,250 --> 00:31:13,625
We work in securities.

582
00:31:14,166 --> 00:31:15,726
We're good at tallying every last cent.

583
00:31:15,958 --> 00:31:16,958
Come on.

584
00:31:27,541 --> 00:31:29,083
Lu Xiaofan, your brother's calling.

585
00:31:40,541 --> 00:31:41,707
I'm just calling to fill you in.

586
00:31:41,708 --> 00:31:43,416
Mom had a phone call with Mr. Bei.

587
00:31:43,458 --> 00:31:44,375
Everyone figures this marriage
won't end in divorce.

588
00:31:45,500 --> 00:31:47,166
Can't you think for once, Lu Xiaofan?

589
00:31:48,083 --> 00:31:48,583
Hey.

590
00:31:48,584 --> 00:31:50,541
Do you never stop to
think about the family?

591
00:31:50,708 --> 00:31:52,726
Mom's blood pressure spiked
so badly she can't get out of bed.

592
00:31:52,750 --> 00:31:54,290
Cut this nonsense, I'm warning you.

593
00:31:54,291 --> 00:31:55,541
Wrap it up and get home now.

594
00:31:56,500 --> 00:31:57,583
I'm not coming back.

595
00:31:58,125 --> 00:31:59,805
Are you trying to give Mom a heart attack?

596
00:31:59,916 --> 00:32:00,916
Cut it out.

597
00:32:01,041 --> 00:32:02,351
I'll head to Lingang in a couple of days.

598
00:32:02,375 --> 00:32:03,375
We'll talk in person.
